{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Let his days be few</b> — R. Joshua said: for his appointment is his wife. But in my opinion: for it is the appointment of all men. And the meaning: that his death should be by the hand of man. And some say: for his appointment is his soul, which is like a pledge."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 109, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:39:11.345697531Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}